<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/music">Music</a> controls what plays through a kiosk's speakers. Start by choosing the kiosk
        (client) at the top. Everything you do then applies to that kiosk.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Playing music">
        <ul>
            <li>On the <strong>Playlists</strong> tab, choose a playlist to see its songs. On <strong>Songs</strong>,
                pick a song to play it.</li>
            <li>The controls at the bottom are <strong>Shuffle</strong>, previous or restart (click once to restart
                the song, twice for the previous one), play and pause, <strong>Next</strong>, and repeat (off, the
                playlist, or the current song).</li>
            <li>Drag the volume slider, or select the speaker to mute.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            While an audio clip is playing over the music, it's shown here with a <strong>Stop</strong> button.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Playlists and songs">
        <FluentText>
            Upload songs in the <a href="/files">File Manager</a>. Audio files are added to the music library
            automatically. Admins and people with the CanManagePlaylists role can create playlists (name and
            optional description) and add songs to them.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
